WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.507
Temperature and top P solve different problems.

00:00:03.507 --> 00:00:11.562
Temperature reshapes the entire probability distribution, while top P keeps only enough high-probability tokens to reach

00:00:11.562 --> 00:00:15.032
a chosen cumulative probability threshold.

00:00:15.032 --> 00:00:20.012
Comparing them on the same distribution makes that distinction much clearer.

00:00:20.012 --> 00:00:25.932
This is why the two settings should not be described as interchangeable creativity controls.

00:00:25.932 --> 00:00:30.960
One reshapes probabilities; the other removes the low-probability tail.
